  "sex6",                  "Eligible by Sex",                          "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who are eligible for LAI ART after being screened, by sex. \n\nTo compare whether clients who are eligible for LAI ART differ from clients who are not eligible for LAI ART for the sex variable, users can compare the bars (eligible for LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., female, male). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients eligible for LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients eligible for LAI ART regardless of sex).",
  "race6",                 "Eligible by Race",                         "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who are eligible for LAI ART after being screened, by race. \n\nTo compare whether clients who are eligible for LAI ART differ from clients who are not eligible for LAI ART for the race variable, users can compare the bars (eligible for LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., Black, White). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients eligible for LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients eligible for LAI ART regardless of race).",
  "ethnicity6",            "Eligible by Ethnicity",                    "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who are eligible for LAI ART after being screened, by ethnicity. \n\nTo compare whether clients who are eligible for LAI ART differ from clients who are not eligible for LAI ART for the ethnicity variable, users can compare the bars (eligible for LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., Hispanic, Not Hispanic). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients eligible for LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients eligible for LAI ART regardless of ethnicity).",
  "age6",                  "Eligible by Age",                          "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who are eligible for LAI ART after being screened, by age. \n\nTo compare whether clients who are eligible for LAI ART differ from clients who are not eligible for LAI ART for the age variable, users can compare the bars (eligible for LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., age 18-24, 25-34). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients eligible for LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients eligible for LAI ART regardless of age).",
  "insurance6",            "Eligible by HIV Medication Payor",         "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who are eligible for LAI ART after being screened, by HIV medication payor. \n\nThe HIV medicator payor variable is created by combining two variables: health_care_coverage (the primary source of health care coverage the client had for any part of the reporting period; includes private insurance, Medicare, Medicaid, Veterans Health Administration, Indian Health Service, other health plans, or no insurance/uninsured) and secondary_payor (the payor of HIV medications if different or supplemental from health care coverage; includes ADAP and patient assistance programs). \n\nTo compare whether clients who are eligible for LAI ART differ from clients who are not eligible for LAI ART for the HIV medicator payor variable, users can compare the bars (eligible for LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., private insurance, uninsured-ADAP). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients eligible for LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients eligible for LAI ART regardless of HIV medication payor).",
  "keypop6",               "Eligible by Key Population",               "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who are eligible for LAI ART after being screened, by key population. \n\nKey populations include patients with different housing or employment status, poverty level, primary language, incarceration history, or other social determinants of health measured by the clinic. \n\nTo compare whether clients who are eligible for LAI ART differ from clients who are not eligible for LAI ART for the key population variable, users can first select a key population (e.g., patients with different housing status) and then compare the bars (eligible for LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., patients with different housing status). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients eligible for LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients eligible for LAI ART regardless of key population).",
  "time6",                 "Eligible Over Time (by person)",           "Eligible over time by person shows the number of people eligible by month, based on their most recent screening date, with the color representing the number eligible/not eligible. \n\u2022 Each person can show up at most 1 time \n\u2022 The date reflects their most recent screening event. If a person was screened multiple times, only the most recent screening event is reflected.",
  "time6_event",           "Eligible Over Time (by encounter)",        "Eligible over time by encounter shows the number of screening events occurring each month. This includes all unique dates when a person was screened. The color represents the number eligible/not eligible. \n\u2022 Each person can show up multiple times \n\u2022 The date reflects the date the screening occurred",
  "not_eligible_reason",   "Reasons Not Eligible",                     "The not eligible reasons plot displays the number and percent reporting each reason among those not eligible at their most recent screening encounter. \n\nNote that interpretation of this chart will depend on how the variable \"not_eligible_reason\" was coded. A clinic could choose to collect the primary reason for non-eligibility or multiple reasons for non-eligibility. If a clinic collected data on multiple reasons for non-eligibility, the interpretation of the plot is as follows: \n\u2022 If the primary reason is reported in the \"reason\" column, and other reasons are reported in the \"other\" column, then the denominator of the bar chart is the number of clients not eligible for iCAB/RPV. \n\u2022 If all not eligible reasons are reported, separated by commas, then the denominator of the bar chart is the total number of reasons provided for non-eligibility among clients not eligible for iCAB/RPV.",
  
  # ========== Prescribed Section ==========
  "prescribed_overall",    "Prescribed Overall",                       "This plot shows the percent of people who have been prescribed LAI ART. The denominator is the number of clients interested and eligible (if counseling and screening are consistently recorded) or all people with HIV at the clinic (if counseling and screening are not consistently recorded).",
  "sex7",                  "Prescribed by Sex",                        "This plot shows the percent of people who have been prescribed LAI ART, by sex. The denominator is the number of clients interested and eligible (if counseling and screening are consistently recorded) or all people with HIV at the clinic (if counseling and screening are not consistently recorded). \n\nTo compare whether clients who were ever prescribed for LAI ART  differ from clients who were never prescribed LAI ART for the sex variable, users can compare the bars (prescribed LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., female, male). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients ever prescribed LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients ever prescribed LAI ART regardless of sex).",
  "race7",                 "Prescribed by Race",                       "This plot shows the percent of people who have been prescribed LAI ART, by race. The denominator is the number of clients interested and eligible (if counseling and screening are consistently recorded) or all people with HIV at the clinic (if counseling and screening are not consistently recorded). \n\nTo compare whether clients who were ever prescribed LAI ART differ from clients who were never prescribed LAI ART for the race variable, users can compare the bars (ever prescribed LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., Black, White). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients ever prescribed LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients ever prescribed LAI ART regardless of race).",
  "ethnicity7",            "Prescribed by Ethnicity",                  "This plot shows the percent of people who have been prescribed LAI ART, by ethnicity. The denominator is the number of clients interested and eligible (if counseling and screening are consistently recorded) or all people with HIV at the clinic (if counseling and screening are not consistently recorded). \n\nTo compare whether clients who were ever prescribed LAI ART differ from clients who were never prescribed LAI ART for the ethnicity variable, users can compare the bars (ever prescribed LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., Hispanic, Not Hispanic). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients ever prescribed LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients ever prescribed LAI ART regardless of ethnicity).",
  "age7",                  "Prescribed by Age",                        "This plot shows the percent of people who have been prescribed LAI ART, by age. The denominator is the number of clients interested and eligible (if counseling and screening are consistently recorded) or all people with HIV at the clinic (if counseling and screening are not consistently recorded). \n\nTo compare whether clients who were ever prescribed LAI ART differ from clients who were never prescribed LAI ART for the age variable, users can compare the bars (ever prescribed LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., age 18-24, 25-34). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients ever prescribed LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients ever prescribed LAI ART regardless of age).",
  "insurance7",            "Prescribed by HIV Medication Payor",       "This plot shows the percent of people who have been prescribed LAI ART, by HIV medication payor. The denominator is the number of clients interested and eligible (if counseling and screening are consistently recorded) or all people with HIV at the clinic (if counseling and screening are not consistently recorded). \n\nThe HIV medicator payor variable is created by combining two variables: health_care_coverage (the primary source of health care coverage the client had for any part of the reporting period; includes private insurance, Medicare, Medicaid, Veterans Health Administration, Indian Health Service, other health plans, or no insurance/uninsured) and secondary_payor (the payor of HIV medications if different or supplemental from health care coverage; includes ADAP and patient assistance programs). \n\nTo compare whether clients who were ever prescribed LAI ART differ from clients who were never prescribed LAI ART for the HIV medicator payor variable, users can compare the bars (ever prescribed LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., private insurance, uninsured-ADAP). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients ever prescribed LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients ever prescribed LAI ART regardless of HIV medication payor).",
  "keypop7",               "Prescribed by Key Population",             "This plot shows the percent of people who have been prescribed LAI ART, by key population. The denominator is the number of clients interested and eligible (if counseling and screening are consistently recorded) or all people with HIV at the clinic (if counseling and screening are not consistently recorded). \n\nKey populations include patients with different housing or employment status, poverty level, primary language, incarceration history, or other social determinants of health measured by the clinic. \n\nTo compare whether clients who were ever prescribed LAI ART differ from clients who were never prescribed LAI ART for the key population variable, users can first select a key population (e.g., patients with different housing status) and then compare the bars (ever prescribed LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., patients with different housing status). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients ever prescribed LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients ever prescribed LAI ART regardless of key population).",
  "time7",                 "Prescribed Over Time",                     "Prescribed over time by person shows the number of people prescribed by month. Each person can show up at most 1 time.",
  
  # ========== Accessible Section ==========
