  "sex7a",                 "Accessible by Sex",                        "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who could financially access LAI ART after being prescribed, by sex. \n\nTo compare whether clients who could financially access LAI ART differ from clients who could not financially access LAI ART for the sex variable, users can compare the bars (accessible LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., female, male). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients who could financially access LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients who could financially access LAI ART regardless of sex).",
  "race7a",                "Accessible by Race",                       "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who could financially access LAI ART after being prescribed, by race. \n\nTo compare whether clients who could financially access LAI ART differ from clients who could not financially access LAI ART for the race variable, users can compare the bars (accessible LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., Black, White). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients who could financially access LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients who could financially access LAI ART regardless of race).",
  "ethnicity7a",           "Accessible by Ethnicity",                  "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who could financially access LAI ART after being prescribed, by ethnicity. \n\nTo compare whether clients who could financially access LAI ART differ from clients who could not financially access LAI ART for the ethnicity variable, users can compare the bars (accessible LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., Hispanic, Not Hispanic). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients who could financially access LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients who could financially access LAI ART regardless of ethnicity).",
  "age7a",                 "Accessible by Age",                        "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who could financially access LAI ART after being prescribed, by age. \n\nTo compare whether clients who could financially access LAI ART differ from clients who could not financially access LAI ART for the age variable, users can compare the bars (accessible LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., age 18-24, 25-34). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients who could financially access LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients who could financially access LAI ART regardless of age).",
  "insurance7a",           "Accessible by HIV Medication Payor",       "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who could financially access LAI ART after being prescribed, by HIV medication payor. \n\nThe HIV medicator payor variable is created by combining two variables: health_care_coverage (the primary source of health care coverage the client had for any part of the reporting period; includes private insurance, Medicare, Medicaid, Veterans Health Administration, Indian Health Service, other health plans, or no insurance/uninsured) and secondary_payor (the payor of HIV medications if different or supplemental from health care coverage; includes ADAP and patient assistance programs). \n\nTo compare whether clients who could financially access LAI ART differ from clients who could not financially access LAI ART for the HIV medicator payor variable, users can compare the bars (accessible LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., private insurance, uninsured-ADAP). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients who could financially access LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients who could financially access LAI ART regardless of HIV medication payor).",
  "keypop7a",              "Accessible by Key Population",             "This plot shows the percent of people with HIV served at your clinic who could financially access LAI ART after being prescribed, by key population. \n\nKey populations include patients with different housing or employment status, poverty level, primary language, incarceration history, or other social determinants of health measured by the clinic. \n\nTo compare whether clients who could financially access LAI ART differ from clients who could not financially access LAI ART for the key population variable, users can first select a key population (e.g., patients with different housing status) and then compare the bars (accessible LAI ART) for each variable category (e.g., patients with different housing status). Differences in these values represent a care gap where one variable category are over or under represented among clients who could financially access LAI ART, relative to their representativeness at the clinic. The dotted line indicates the clinic average (patients who could financially access LAI ART regardless of key population).",
  "time7a",                "Accessible Over Time",                     "Accessible over time shows the number of clients who could financially access LAI ART by prescription month. The height of the bar represents the number of clients prescribed, and the color represents whether LAI ART was financially accessible or not.",
  "not_accessible_reason", "Reasons Not Accessible",                   "Not accessible reasons plot displays the number and percent reporting each reason among those who could not financially access LAI ART when prescribed. \n\nNote that interpretation of this chart will depend on how the variable \"not_accessible_reason\" was coded. A clinic could choose to collect the primary reason for non-accessibility or multiple reasons for non-accessibility. If a clinic collected data on multiple reasons for non-accessibility, the interpretation of the plot is as follows: \n\u2022 If the primary reason is reported in the \"reason\" column, and other reasons are reported in the \"other\" column, then the denominator of the bar chart is the number of clients who could not access iCAB/RPV. \n\u2022 If all not accessible reasons are reported, separated by commas, then the denominator of the bar chart is the total number of reasons provided for non-accessibility among clients who could not access iCAB/RPV.",
  
